# State, Providers, Error Handling & Performance

## Zustand — Global State

Use Zustand for global client state only — auth token, UI preferences, cart, etc.
Do NOT put server data in Zustand — that belongs in React Query.

```typescript
// src/store/auth.store.ts
import { create } from "zustand";
import { persist } from "zustand/middleware";

interface AuthState {
  token: string | null;
  setToken: (token: string) => void;
  clearToken: () => void;
}

export const useAuthStore = create<AuthState>()(
  persist(
    (set) => ({
      token: null,
      setToken: (token) => set({ token }),
      clearToken: () => set({ token: null }),
    }),
    { name: "auth-storage" }
  )
);
```

```typescript
// src/store/ui.store.ts
import { create } from "zustand";

interface UIState {
  sidebarOpen: boolean;
  toggleSidebar: () => void;
}

export const useUIStore = create<UIState>((set) => ({
  sidebarOpen: true,
  toggleSidebar: () => set((state) => ({ sidebarOpen: !state.sidebarOpen })),
}));
```

---

## What Goes Where

| Data type | Where |
|---|---|
| Server data (products, users) | React Query |
| Auth token, user session | Zustand + persist |
| UI state (sidebar, theme) | Zustand |
| Form state | React Hook Form |
| URL state (filters, pagination) | TanStack Router search params |
| Component-local state | useState |

