## Sonner Toast Patterns

```typescript
import { toast } from "sonner";

// Success
toast.success("Product created");

// Error — always in mutation onError
toast.error(getErrorMessage(error));

// With description
toast.error("Upload failed", {
  description: "File size must be under 5MB",
});

// Promise — for async with loading state
toast.promise(saveProduct(data), {
  loading: "Saving...",
  success: "Saved!",
  error: "Failed to save",
});
```

Rules:
- Toast calls go in mutation callbacks — never inside render or useEffect
- Always use `getErrorMessage(error)` — never hardcode error strings in `onError`

