## Performance — Code Splitting

Use `React.lazy` + `Suspense` for route-level and heavy component code splitting:

```typescript
import { lazy, Suspense } from "react";

const HeavyComponent = lazy(
  () => import("@/features/analytics/components/HeavyChart")
);

<Suspense fallback={<ChartSkeleton />}>
  <HeavyComponent />
</Suspense>
```

---

## Rules Summary

- ✅ Zustand for global client state only — server data stays in React Query
- ✅ All providers grouped in `app-providers.tsx`
- ✅ Services throw `AppError` — never generic `Error`
- ✅ `getErrorMessage()` in all `onError` callbacks
- ✅ Toast calls in mutation callbacks only — never in render
- ✅ `import.meta.env.VITE_*` for env vars — never `process.env`
- ✅ `React.lazy` + `Suspense` for code splitting
- ❌ Never put server data in Zustand
- ❌ Never leave `console.log` in committed code
